/addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHMAWARI NAGASHIGE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ONO PHARMACEUTICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUI, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHMAWARI, NAGASHIGE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ONO PHARMACEUTICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUI TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHMAWARI NAGASHIGE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUI, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHMAWARI, NAGASHIGE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Phosphoric acid derivatives represented by general formula (I), wherein each symbol is as defined in the description, and nontoxic salts thereof. Because of having a TNF alpha  production inhibitory effect, the compounds represented by general formula (I) are useful as preventives and/or remedies for rheumatoid arthritis, ulcerative colitis, Crohn's disease, hepatitis, sepsis, hemorrhagic shock, multiple sclerosis, brain infarction, diabetes, interstitial pneumonia, uveitis, pain, glomerulonephritis, HIV-associated diseases, cachexia, myocardial infarction, chronic heart failure, oral aphtha, Hansen's disease, infection, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne, d'une part des dérivés d'acide phosphorique représentés par la formule générale (I) suivante, et d'autre part certains de leurs sels non toxiques. Dans cette formule, chacun des symboles est tel que défini dans la description. En raison de leur action inhibitrice sur la production du TNF alpha , les composés représentés par la formule générale (I) conviennent pour le traitement curatif et/ou préventif d'affections telles que polyarthrite rhumatoïde, colite ulcéreuse, maladie de Crohn, hépatite, septicémie, choc hémorragique, sclérose en plaques, infarctus cérébral, diabètes, pneumonie interstitielle, uvéite, douleur, glomérulonéphrite, pathologies associées au VIH, cachexie, infarctus du myocarde, insuffisance cardiaque chronique, aphtes, maladie de Hansen, infections.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>